  "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{e}^{xy}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{1\\cdot y}-{e}^{0\\cdot y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y}-y]_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =({e}^{4}-4)-({e}^{0}-0)\\text{\u00a0} \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-4-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
